.TH mnnn-notify 1  "mnnn-notify 2.18.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-notify \- Notifications: what built\-in events, rule sets (`then notify`) and broadcasts from other nodes tell you; read, unread and muted by kind. Synced to linked nodes
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn notify\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Notifications: what built\-in events, rule sets (`then notify`) and broadcasts from other nodes tell you; read, unread and muted by kind. Synced to linked nodes
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH NOTES
.PP
Built\-in events notify you: exchange requests, org applications, review comments, suggestions and votes from peers, sync conflicts, org code syncs, broadcasts and messages. A rule set's `notify TITLE [body=..] [link=..] [level=info|warn|error]` makes one too, and each notification is itself a `notification` action rules can trigger on. Links point at context: review:ID, org:ID, messages:PEER, live:SESSION, journal:ID, project:ID, search:ID, rule:ID, action:ID. `mnnn help notifications` has the guide.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mnnn\-notify\-list(1)
Notifications, newest first
.TP
mnnn\-notify\-show(1)
Show one (id or unique prefix) and mark it read
.TP
mnnn\-notify\-read(1)
Mark one, or all, read
.TP
mnnn\-notify\-unread(1)
Mark one unread again
.TP
mnnn\-notify\-send(1)
Send yourself one (handy in scripts)
.TP
mnnn\-notify\-kinds(1)
The built\-in kinds and whether each is muted
.TP
mnnn\-notify\-mute(1)
Stop a built\-in kind from notifying
.TP
mnnn\-notify\-unmute(1)
Let a muted kind notify again
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.18.0
.SH SEE ALSO
